{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546115-what-book-have-the-kuei-jin-interact-with-the-imbue","id":1546115,"title":"What book have the Kuei Jin interact with the Imbue?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-18T22:45:55-08:00","id":1546115,"title":"What book have the Kuei Jin interact with the Imbue?","content":"I feel like it was a miss potential have them not interact that much within the lore, when they're so similiar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T23:25:14-08:00","id":1546116,"title":"","content":"Most notably, The Walking Dead, with the character Ichmail. I think there are some other notes scattered around in places, like the Hunter Survival Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T00:27:23-08:00","id":1546118,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that at first the Imbued and the Wan Kuei were going to have a lot of lore in common, but it was linked to the idea that the WoD and Exalted were linked settings as well.<br /> <br /> When the Exalted-as-prehistory angle was discarded, a lot of the hints at how the Wan Kuei and Imbued's lore are intertwined went with it.<br /> <br /> That said, a good deal remains. The &quot;secret&quot; section of the ST Companion that details the truth about the Imbued makes some heavy links to the lore of the KotE books, as does Hunter: Apocrypha. The simple version is that the Wan Kuei are most likely corrupted remnants of the last time the Messengers went around Imbuing people; which came with way more power, and lead to decadence and a fallen from grace. Thus a driving factor on why the Imbued in modern times were made significantly weaker so they couldn't accumulate power on the same scale again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-30T19:39:02-08:00","id":1546507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546115-what-book-have-the-kuei-jin-interact-with-the-imbue#post1546115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like it was a miss potential have them not interact that much within the lore, when they're so similiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's no reason for the Heralds to skip imbuing folks in the Middle Kingdom, so they'd certainly have their hands full with ALL the creatures there, including the Beast Courts and the Hsien, as well! I really don't see them as being that similar to the Kuei-Jin, tho...<br /> <br /> If anything, I'd have liked to see more interaction between the Wan Kuei and the Fallen! It'd really be interesting to see Demons inhabiting Asian people's bodies and perhaps even having their identities filtered through Eastern cultural stories, like a Devil whose Revelatory form is more Shiva/Kali than Angelic/Demonic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T01:05:41-08:00","id":1546530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1546115-what-book-have-the-kuei-jin-interact-with-the-imbue?p=1546118#post1546118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When the Exalted-as-prehistory angle was discarded, a lot of the hints at how the Wan Kuei and Imbued's lore are intertwined went with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and No. The Exalted-as-prehistory thing was only thrown out fully by Exalted. WoD has too much lore tied into that early development to remove it completely, so it's more of a Schrodinger's Lore situation. Exalted being the WoD's past is just as true as the Fallen's version of pre-history, as is the Garou/Mokole/Ananasi's version of pre-history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T03:58:55-08:00","id":1546533,"title":"","content":"It was fully thrown out by both games. Exalted as the pre-history of the WoD means nothing to Demon. They're written explicitly as Milton-esque fallen angels that rebelled against a Christian take on the divine. They don't need Exalted to exist at all to make sense in their own lore. The games of the WoD that started in 1e were created before Exalted was an idea, and it was Exalted that took cues from them that created the links between the games. The cycle of ages was in the WoD first. The Dragon Kings predating the dominance of humanity was written years before GCG wrote the first treatments for Exalted. The WoD's lore doesn't need Exalted for anything. KotE and HtR were the closest because they were developed when the idea was going around, but that was all rewritten to make sense without it.<br /> <br /> The WoD certain has a &quot;Scrodinger's Lore.&quot; But it had that from the beginning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T11:53:07-08:00","id":1546596,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the original conception of Exalted was that you played the Elementally-powered Wan Xian, in the Middle Kingdom's Age before they were corrupted by the Yama Kings, and your PCs fought demons with the early Beast Courts, Hsien, etc as your allies or enemies...Then Grabowski came on board and shifted it to another world that MIGHT be related to the WoD, and the Wan Xian evolved into the Dragon-Blooded/Solars...As thrilled as I was for it at the time, I'm way over it, and now want both games to be as separate as possible, I'd honestly prefer if newer editions of Exalted even got rid of WoD-loaded terms like &quot;Paradox&quot;, for ex.<br /> <br /> But, man, that WX game idea STILL sounds like a great game setting, shame they didn't at least put out a supplement for it! Did anyone ever make a fan version of that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}